{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794828455,"nonce":"bgtORnBJdTI5nrMYB9d5bWJ9JQk=","message":"Found while testing hxn-gpu's WebGPU-to-WebGL2 fallback under Ash 0.1.19 (Chrome with --disable-features=WebGPUService, so no WebGPU). The program hangs and prints nothing. The Ash session traced it (ash-ba):\n- The agent's requestAdapter resolves with no adapter when the browser returns null, instead of rejecting. The program then sends requestDevice on the unset handle. gpu_webgpu_service.mjs throws a TypeError there, and its serve loop passes it to wire.error, which only calls console.error. The op gets no reply, so the program waits forever. Under hxcpp the same case rejects ('requestAdapter returned null') and the fallback works.\n- gpu_webgpu.mjs's start() calls canvas.transferControlToOffscreen(), as gpu_webgl2.mjs's does. Whichever agent starts first takes the canvas, so a page carrying both cannot fall back from one to the other.\nFixes for 0.2.0: reject requestAdapter on null; have the generated service loop (x-idl) reply with an error when an op throws; transfer the canvas on first use (createCanvasSurface), not in start(). Ash will separately fail a page whose agent op throws without replying.","files":null}]}